          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"100nF\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"VO\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C1 +5V 0 100n"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The LM1117 output may become unstable or oscillate, causing the +5V rail to be unreliable and potentially leading to MCU resets or erratic fan-control behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The main supported anomaly is the LM1117-5.0 output capacitor value: +5V has only a 100nF capacitor, while standard practice and the regulator datasheet require a much larger output capacitor for stability."
}

